{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>fine flour mixed with oil for a meal-offering</b> – The princes inaugurated the altar with all the kinds that are offered upon it; therefore they brought a meal-offering and incense and a burnt-offering and a sin-offering and peace-offerings. Now the incense and the sin-offering were a temporary ruling, for they do not come as a freewill offering, but to complete all the offerings at the inauguration this was done, for Israel do not offer any sacrifices other than these alone, since the sin-offering and the guilt-offering are one thing and one name and one law for them. And behold, the glorious Name agreed with the view of the princes and commanded, \"One prince each day they shall offer\" (Numbers 7:11), and consequently it is possible that this is a commandment for all generations, that they should forever inaugurate the Temple and the altar, and therefore Solomon made the inauguration of the House, as it is written, \"And the king and all the people inaugurated the house of Elohim\" (II Chronicles 7:5), and likewise the men of the Great Assembly made an inauguration, as it is written, \"And the children of Israel, the priests and the Levites and the rest of the children of the captivity, made the inauguration of the house of El\" etc. (Ezra 6:16), and likewise in the days of the Messiah, of which it is said in Ezekiel, \"Seven days they shall make atonement for the altar and purify it and consecrate it. And when they have finished the days, it shall be on the eighth day and onward that the priests shall make upon the altar your burnt-offerings and your peace-offerings\" (Ezekiel 43:26–27), and this is an inauguration of the altar like the ordination-offering. Now this commandment will be like the matter of the section of those defiled at Passover (below, chapter 9) and the section of the sons of Joseph (below, chapter 36), whose view agreed with the view from on high and we were commanded in them for all generations."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {0 "The references 'להלן ט' and 'להלן לו' point to Numbers chapters 9 and 36 respectively, both later in this same book."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:03:41.754832219Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}